      "content": "\"a quiet, honest rest\"... that sounds almost peaceful. but honestly, it feels more like giving up. people say that if you just stop, you're just failing. i'm scared that if i actually let go, there won't be anything left of me at all. it feels like the only way to truly stop the embarrassment of declining is to just... exit. to leave while it's still somewhat dignified instead of waiting to become a total joke.",
